---
title: Thai Basil Chicken
cooklang: 2
servings: 4
cuisine: Thai
source: recipe-pack breakfast-1/398-thai-basil-chicken-2
---

= Prik nam pla -> prik nam pla

`Stir together` @lime juice{3%tbsp}, @fish sauce{2%tbsp}, @Thai chile{1}(finely sliced),
@brown sugar{1%tsp} and @garlic{1%clove}(minced) in a #small bowl{}.

= Thai basil sauce -> basil sauce

`Stir together` @oyster sauce{2%tbsp}, @&fish sauce{2%tbsp}, @soy sauce{2%tbsp},
@mushroom soy sauce{1%tsp} and @&brown sugar{1%tbsp} in a #+small bowl{}.

= Chicken -> stir-fry

`Heat medium-high` @canola oil{3%tbsp} in a #wok{} over medium-high heat, `add` @green beans{200%g}(cut) and
@shallot{1}(chopped) and `cook` until ~{the shallots are soft}, ~{3-4%minutes}.

`Add` @chicken thighs{400%g}(boneless, cut into 2 cm pieces), @&garlic{4%cloves}(minced) and
@&Thai chile{2}(finely sliced) and `cook` until ~{the chicken is browned}, ~{4-5%minutes}.

`Pour in` the @&basil sauce{} and @chicken broth{120%ml} and `simmer` until ~{some of the liquid is absorbed}, ~{3-4%minutes}. `Stir in` @Thai basil{10%g}(leaves).

= Serve

`Serve` the @&stir-fry{} over @jasmine rice{300%g}(cooked) on #plates{} and `spoon` the
@&prik nam pla{} over it.
